{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P7Um9EXshr9gevibUz5MpT","type":"tool_result","content":"200\t        project=project,\n201\t    )\n202\t\n203\t\n204\tdef emit_pair_rail_outgoing_redaction_applied(\n205\t    *,\n206\t    signal: str = \"\",\n207\t    family: str = \"\",\n208\t    match_count: int = 0,\n209\t    bytes_scanned: int = 0,\n210\t    callsite: str = \"\",\n211\t    session_id: str = \"\",\n212\t    project: str = \"\",\n213\t    atlas_technique: Optional[str] = None,\n214\t) -> None:\n215\t    \"\"\"Emit pair_rail_outgoing_redaction_applied (ADR-114; F-7.9 positive proof).\n216\t\n217\t    The OUTBOUND pair-rail egress redactor (framework → Codex/external LLM)\n218\t    scrubbed the outgoing prompt. Emitted on EVERY redaction call, INCLUDING\n219\t    when the findings list is empty (``match_count=0`` is positive proof the\n220\t    redaction path was exercised). Content-field-free per Sec MF-3 — the\n221\t    dispatch gate routes through _PAIR_RAIL_OUTGOING_REDACTION_APPLIED_ALLOWLIST\n222\t    which excludes ``text``/``prompt``/``match_value``. Mirrors\n223\t    ``emit_codex_egress_redacted``'s signature.\n224\t    \"\"\"\n225\t    emit_generic(\n226\t        \"pair_rail_outgoing_redaction_applied\",\n227\t        atlas_technique=atlas_technique or \"AML.T0054\",\n228\t        signal=signal,\n229\t        family=family,\n230\t        match_count=int(match_count),\n231\t        bytes_scanned=int(bytes_scanned),\n232\t        callsite=callsite,\n233\t        session_id=session_id,\n234\t        project=project,\n235\t    )\n236\t\n237\t\n238\tdef emit_mcp_handler_invoked(\n239\t    handler: str,\n240\t    client_id: str,\n241\t    transport: str,\n242\t    duration_ms: int,\n243\t    session_id: str = \"\",\n244\t    project: str = \"\",\n245\t) -> None:\n246\t    \"\"\"Emit a mcp_handler_invoked event (ADR-042 §Auth).\n247\t\n248\t    Fired on every successful handler entry AFTER auth + ACL + rate-limit\n249\t    pass. ``client_id`` is the 16-hex opaque identifier (never the token\n250\t    itself). ``transport`` ∈ {\"http\", \"stdio\"}. ``handler`` ∈ the 7 handler\n251\t    names registered in ADR-042 §Auth.2 ACL.\n252\t    \"\"\"\n253\t    event: Dict[str, Any] = {\n254\t        \"action\": \"mcp_handler_invoked\",\n255\t        \"handler\": handler,\n256\t        \"client_id\": client_id,\n257\t        \"transport\": transport,\n258\t        \"duration_ms\": int(duration_ms),\n259\t        \"session_id\": session_id,\n260\t        \"project\": project,\n261\t    }\n262\t    _write_event(event)\n263\t\n264\t\n265\tdef emit_mcp_handler_denied(\n266\t    handler: str,\n267\t    client_id: str,\n268\t    transport: str,\n269\t    reason: str,\n270\t    session_id: str = \"\",\n271\t    project: str = \"\",\n272\t) -> None:\n273\t    \"\"\"Emit a mcp_handler_denied event (ADR-042 §Auth.5).\n274\t\n275\t    ``reason`` is the closed enum: acl_missing_handler | rate_limit |\n276\t    timestamp_skew | cors_default_deny | auth_hmac_invalid |\n277\t    auth_token_malformed | budget_hard_stop_per_spawn |\n278\t    budget_hard_stop_per_plan_5min | debate_max_rounds | breaker_open |\n279\t    plan_id_unknown. Token value MUST NOT appear anywhere (ADR-042\n280\t    §Auth.6 hygiene).\n281\t    \"\"\"\n282\t    event: Dict[str, Any] = {\n283\t        \"action\": \"mcp_handler_denied\",\n284\t        \"handler\": handler,\n285\t        \"client_id\": client_id,\n286\t        \"transport\": transport,\n287\t        \"reason\": reason,\n288\t        \"session_id\": session_id,\n289\t        \"project\": project,\n290\t    }\n291\t    _write_event(event)\n292\t\n293\t\n294\tdef emit_mcp_cross_tenant_denied(\n295\t    handler: str,\n296\t    caller_client_id_hash: str,\n297\t    target_client_id_hash: str,\n298\t    transport: str,\n299\t    session_id: str = \"\",\n300\t    project: str = \"\",\n301\t) -> None:\n302\t    \"\"\"Emit a mcp_cross_tenant_denied event (ADR-042-AMEND-1 §6.2).\n303\t\n304\t    Fires when a get_cost_budget call with scope=caller attempts to\n305\t    read a target_client_id different from the caller's own. The\n306\t    caller/target identifiers are HASHED via auth.hash_client_id\n307\t    before serialization (Sec MF-3 hygiene).\n308\t    \"\"\"\n309\t    event: Dict[str, Any] = {\n310\t        \"action\": \"mcp_cross_tenant_denied\",\n311\t        \"handler\": handler,\n312\t        \"caller_client_id_hash\": caller_client_id_hash,\n313\t        \"target_client_id_hash\": target_client_id_hash,\n314\t        \"transport\": transport,\n315\t        \"session_id\": session_id,\n316\t        \"project\": project,\n317\t    }\n318\t    _write_event(event)\n319\t\n320\t\n321\tdef emit_mcp_soak_fpr_breach(\n322\t    window_days: int,\n323\t    fpr_observed: float,\n324\t    threshold: float,\n325\t    top_deny_reason: str,\n326\t    session_id: str = \"\",\n327\t    project: str = \"\",\n328\t) -> None:\n329\t    \"\"\"Emit a mcp_soak_fpr_breach event (ADR-042-AMEND-1 §6.2 / AC-F-4).\n330\t\n331\t    Fires when 7-day rolling FPR > threshold (default 0.01 = 1%).\n332\t    Fires AT MOST once per breach day; the soak monitor enforces\n333\t    dedup against the most recent emit.\n334\t\n335\t    Float fields are encoded as integers to satisfy the canonical_json\n336\t    no-float invariant on HMAC-covered audit events:\n337\t\n338\t    - ``fpr_observed``  → ``fpr_observed_bps``  (rate × 10000, 0..10000+)\n339\t    - ``threshold``     → ``threshold_bps``     (rate × 10000, 0..10000+)\n340\t\n341\t    Example: FPR 0.01 (1%) → 100 bps; threshold 0.01 → 100 bps.\n342\t    Readers must divide by 10000 to recover the original rate.\n343\t    \"\"\"\n344\t    event: Dict[str, Any] = {\n345\t        \"action\": \"mcp_soak_fpr_breach\",\n346\t        \"window_days\": int(window_days),\n347\t        \"fpr_observed_bps\": max(0, int(round(float(fpr_observed) * 10000))),\n348\t        \"threshold_bps\": max(0, int(round(float(threshold) * 10000))),\n349\t        \"top_deny_reason\": str(top_deny_reason),\n350\t        \"session_id\": session_id,\n351\t        \"project\": project,\n352\t    }\n353\t    _write_event(event)\n354\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05d43db1-9d87-44b2-ba52-8d3e41e19567","uuid":"543c6b47-eff7-4b3f-9da8-0a91e2844888","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:58:45.917Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":".claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/security.py","content":"        project=project,\n    )\n\n\ndef emit_pair_rail_outgoing_redaction_applied(\n    *,\n    signal: str = \"\",\n    family: str = \"\",\n    match_count: int = 0,\n    bytes_scanned: int = 0,\n    callsite: str = \"\",\n    session_id: str = \"\",\n    project: str = \"\",\n    atlas_technique: Optional[str] = None,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Emit pair_rail_outgoing_redaction_applied (ADR-114; F-7.9 positive proof).\n\n    The OUTBOUND pair-rail egress redactor (framework → Codex/external LLM)\n    scrubbed the outgoing prompt. Emitted on EVERY redaction call, INCLUDING\n    when the findings list is empty (``match_count=0`` is positive proof the\n    redaction path was exercised). Content-field-free per Sec MF-3 — the\n    dispatch gate routes through _PAIR_RAIL_OUTGOING_REDACTION_APPLIED_ALLOWLIST\n    which excludes ``text``/``prompt``/``match_value``. Mirrors\n    ``emit_codex_egress_redacted``'s signature.\n    \"\"\"\n    emit_generic(\n        \"pair_rail_outgoing_redaction_applied\",\n        atlas_technique=atlas_technique or \"AML.T0054\",\n        signal=signal,\n        family=family,\n        match_count=int(match_count),\n        bytes_scanned=int(bytes_scanned),\n        callsite=callsite,\n        session_id=session_id,\n        project=project,\n    )\n\n\ndef emit_mcp_handler_invoked(\n    handler: str,\n    client_id: str,\n    transport: str,\n    duration_ms: int,\n    session_id: str = \"\",\n    project: str = \"\",\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Emit a mcp_handler_invoked event (ADR-042 §Auth).\n\n    Fired on every successful handler entry AFTER auth + ACL + rate-limit\n    pass. ``client_id`` is the 16-hex opaque identifier (never the token\n    itself). ``transport`` ∈ {\"http\", \"stdio\"}. ``handler`` ∈ the 7 handler\n    names registered in ADR-042 §Auth.2 ACL.\n    \"\"\"\n    event: Dict[str, Any] = {\n        \"action\": \"mcp_handler_invoked\",\n        \"handler\": handler,\n        \"client_id\": client_id,\n        \"transport\": transport,\n        \"duration_ms\": int(duration_ms),\n        \"session_id\": session_id,\n        \"project\": project,\n    }\n    _write_event(event)\n\n\ndef emit_mcp_handler_denied(\n    handler: str,\n    client_id: str,\n    transport: str,\n    reason: str,\n    session_id: str = \"\",\n    project: str = \"\",\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Emit a mcp_handler_denied event (ADR-042 §Auth.5).\n\n    ``reason`` is the closed enum: acl_missing_handler | rate_limit |\n    timestamp_skew | cors_default_deny | auth_hmac_invalid |\n    auth_token_malformed | budget_hard_stop_per_spawn |\n    budget_hard_stop_per_plan_5min | debate_max_rounds | breaker_open |\n    plan_id_unknown. Token value MUST NOT appear anywhere (ADR-042\n    §Auth.6 hygiene).\n    \"\"\"\n    event: Dict[str, Any] = {\n        \"action\": \"mcp_handler_denied\",\n        \"handler\": handler,\n        \"client_id\": client_id,\n        \"transport\": transport,\n        \"reason\": reason,\n        \"session_id\": session_id,\n        \"project\": project,\n    }\n    _write_event(event)\n\n\ndef emit_mcp_cross_tenant_denied(\n    handler: str,\n    caller_client_id_hash: str,\n    target_client_id_hash: str,\n    transport: str,\n    session_id: str = \"\",\n    project: str = \"\",\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Emit a mcp_cross_tenant_denied event (ADR-042-AMEND-1 §6.2).\n\n    Fires when a get_cost_budget call with scope=caller attempts to\n    read a target_client_id different from the caller's own. The\n    caller/target identifiers are HASHED via auth.hash_client_id\n    before serialization (Sec MF-3 hygiene).\n    \"\"\"\n    event: Dict[str, Any] = {\n        \"action\": \"mcp_cross_tenant_denied\",\n        \"handler\": handler,\n        \"caller_client_id_hash\": caller_client_id_hash,\n        \"target_client_id_hash\": target_client_id_hash,\n        \"transport\": transport,\n        \"session_id\": session_id,\n        \"project\": project,\n    }\n    _write_event(event)\n\n\ndef emit_mcp_soak_fpr_breach(\n    window_days: int,\n    fpr_observed: float,\n    threshold: float,\n    top_deny_reason: str,\n    session_id: str = \"\",\n    project: str = \"\",\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Emit a mcp_soak_fpr_breach event (ADR-042-AMEND-1 §6.2 / AC-F-4).\n\n    Fires when 7-day rolling FPR > threshold (default 0.01 = 1%).\n    Fires AT MOST once per breach day; the soak monitor enforces\n    dedup against the most recent emit.\n\n    Float fields are encoded as integers to satisfy the canonical_json\n    no-float invariant on HMAC-covered audit events:\n\n    - ``fpr_observed``  → ``fpr_observed_bps``  (rate × 10000, 0..10000+)\n    - ``threshold``     → ``threshold_bps``     (rate × 10000, 0..10000+)\n\n    Example: FPR 0.01 (1%) → 100 bps; threshold 0.01 → 100 bps.\n    Readers must divide by 10000 to recover the original rate.\n    \"\"\"\n    event: Dict[str, Any] = {\n        \"action\": \"mcp_soak_fpr_breach\",\n        \"window_days\": int(window_days),\n        \"fpr_observed_bps\": max(0, int(round(float(fpr_observed) * 10000))),\n        \"threshold_bps\": max(0, int(round(float(threshold) * 10000))),\n        \"top_deny_reason\": str(top_deny_reason),\n        \"session_id\": session_id,\n        \"project\": project,\n    }\n    _write_event(event)\n","numLines":155,"startLine":200,"totalLines":354}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01P7Um9EXshr9gevibUz5MpT","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
