{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch77yK2KMRQynBRfUkY3R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found no P0, no new P1 and no declared condition that is false for payload 16/34, so my decision is GO.\n\n**Scope.** This payload only removes code from `.claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py`. The removed code is:\n- the tail of `emit_pair_rail_outgoing_redaction_applied`;\n- the MCP, RAG, GOAP, MCP-server, policy, replay, prediction, pattern and threat-model emitters;\n- `iter_events`;\n- the whole `emit_generic` dispatch chain;\n- the session, prompt and output-scan emitters;\n- the audit-tokens and tool-lifecycle allowlists;\n- the codex, grok, council, pair-rail, directory, notification, night-mode and learning-loop enums and helpers;\n- the git-bypass, env-hijack, egress, adversary, persistent-instruction, hint, settings-tamper, ceremony-lint and salt allowlists;\n- the ledger enums, up to the start of `_ledger_int_field`.\n\nUnder condition 7 this code moves to `.claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/`, so I checked the deletion against where it now lives in the candidate tree. The GA-only condition says the code is byte-identical to rc.1; I could not check that myself here.\n\n**What I checked against the candidate tree**\n\n1. **The `emit_generic` dispatch.** The facade (`audit_emit.py:473-480`) hands off to `_dispatch_generic` (`generic_dispatch_05.py:361-377`).\n   - Every removed `elif` branch comes back in the same order, across `generic_dispatch_01.py` to `_05.py`.\n   - Each branch ends with `state[\"event\"] = event; return True`, so no branch writes the unscrubbed event.\n   - The three branches that drop the whole event still return `None`, so nothing is written: `persona_coverage_synthesized` (`_01.py:436-450`), `tier_policy_loader_fallback_observed` (`_03.py:92-96`) and `audit_producer_path_pollution_detected` (`_03.py:109-126`).\n   - The passthrough set is still checked last (`_05.py:352`). Default-deny still writes only `{\"action\": action}` plus a breadcrumb (`_05.py:375-377`).\n   - Value coercions match the removed text line by line. I checked:\n     - `ledger_entry_rejected`, `settings_tamper_detected`, `salt_rotation_registered` and `ceremony_lint_unlock_used`;\n     - `pair_rail_case` and `pair_rail_review_expected`, with `_coerce_pair_rail_timeout_ms`;\n     - `credential_override_late_set_ignored`, `swarm_paused_owner_absent`, `mcp_injection_finding` and `session_memory_delta_observed`;\n     - the codex, grok and council branches, the lesson and learning branches, `statusline_sidecar_write`, `model_refusal_observed` and `admin_key_lifecycle_event`.\n   - The fail-open `try/except` around the side emits of `emit_task_route_key_dropped` and `emit_reality_ledger_key_dropped` is kept (`_02.py:29-37`, `:132-140`).\n2. **Every name resolves.** Each name the moved branches use is defined in a part that lists it in `__all__`, and `install()` (`_audit_emit_parts/__init__.py:20-48`) publishes and rebinds only names in `__all__`. I checked `harness_schemas.py:10`, `lifecycle_schemas.py:9`, `compaction.py:8`, `security.py:8`, `planning.py:8` and `replay.py:8`, plus `tokens_boot.py` (`_is_sha256_hex`, the tool-lifecycle enums), `context_pressure.py`, `federation_schemas.py` (passthrough and reserved sets, admin and statusline caps), `adapters.py`, `writer.py` and `finalization.py`. So I found no path that would raise a `NameError` and break `emit_generic`'s never-raises contract.\n3. **Constant values match the removed text.** These include `_LEDGER_ID_RE`, `_LEDGER_GATE_FAMILIES` and `_LEDGER_GATE_REASONS`, `_PAIR_RAIL_REVIEW_ID_RE` (exactly 16 hex or empty), `_PAIR_RAIL_FILE_HASH_PREFIX_RE`, `_PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_MS_MAX=6_000_000`, the 12-hex directory, notification and hostname regexes, `_LEARNING_ID_RE`, `_LESSON_SHA256_RE`, `_EGRESS_DEST_MAX_LEN=253` and `_coerce_egress_destination`.\n4. **Moved code still behaves the same (item 4).**\n   - `install()` binds each part function to the facade's globals, so patches on `audit_emit._write_event`, `_breadcrumb`, `_log_path` and the rest still take effect.\n   - The locks stay in the facade (`audit_emit.py:483-484`), so `deepcopy` never touches them.\n   - `iter_events` is still a lazy generator through the `SimpleNamespace` hop (`audit_emit.py:455-461`), and `replay.py` is the only part that exports it.\n   - `typing` names the facade doesn't import (`Iterator`, `List`) appear only in annotations, which are not evaluated under `from __future__ import annotations` or as local-variable annotations.\n   - The spool-writer forensic emitter and the exit-handler hookup still run at import (`audit_emit.py:486-496`).\n5. **Python 3.9 and standard library only.** The destination code uses no 3.10+ syntax and no third-party imports. `FunctionType(code, globals, name, defaults, closure)` works on 3.9.\n6. **Condition 5.** `check_arbitration_kernel.py:312` lists `.claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/*`, and the facade itself is at `:105`.\n7. **Condition 7 holds for `audit_emit`.** The entry-point path is unchanged and the logic lives in `_lib/_audit_emit_parts/`.\n8. **Fail direction (item 2).** Unchanged: the audit emit path still fails open, and default-deny still drops caller fields instead of writing them. For adopters (item 1), this payload disables no hook and changes no model or effort.\n\n**Conclusion.** No declared condition is false against this payload, and I found no P0.\n\n**NEW FINDINGS (annex):** None at P1.\n\n**P2 follow-ups.** P2-1 to P2-3 were already recorded at P2 in the signed rc.1 verdict `claude-rc1-15`. They are still present in this tree with nothing fixed. P2-4 is new.\n\n- **P2-1. Decoy branches make two structure tests pass vacuously.**\n  - Where: `.claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:473-480`.\n  - Scenario: the facade's `emit_generic` has `if action == \"tool_call_lifecycle_recorded\"` and `if action == \"settings_tamper_detected\"`, which do exactly what the fall-through line does. They exist only so that `inspect.getsource(audit_emit.emit_generic)` contains those comparisons, which `.claude/hooks/tests/test_tool_lifecycle.py:541-563` and `.claude/scripts/tests/test_ceo_boot_tamper_tripwires.py:521-525` require.\n  - The real scrub branches are `generic_dispatch_04.py:62` and `:159`. If they are deleted, both tests stay green; the event would then hit default-deny, so fields would be lost, not leaked.\n  - The ghost-action guard test was updated correctly to walk `_GENERIC_DISPATCH_HANDLERS`.\n  - Minimal fix: remove the decoys and make the two tests call `emit_generic` with a forbidden field, then assert the field is dropped and the enum values are coerced.\n- **P2-2. A second, unused action registry.**\n  - Where: `.claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/actions.py:7-16`, with `actions_core.py` and `actions_extended.py` (331 names).\n  - Scenario: the `install()` list doesn't include these files (`audit_emit.py:415-452`); the runtime registry is the literal at `audit_emit.py:45-377`. A maintainer who registers a new action in `actions_core.py`, which `.claude/scripts/env-inventory.json` points at, gets no runtime effect, and the action is silently dropped as unknown.\n  - Minimal fix: delete `actions*.py`, or add a test that pins them equal to the facade's literal.\n- **P2-3. The unknown-action breadcrumb lost its escaping and can now raise.**\n  - Where: `.claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/generic_dispatch_05.py:363`.\n  - Scenario: the removed code logged `f\"emit_generic: unknown action {action!r}\"`; the new code logs `\"unknown audit action dropped: %s\" % action`.\n  - An action string with a newline is written raw into `audit-log.errors`, which is not HMAC-chained, so lines there can be forged.\n  - A tuple action is hashable, fails the membership test, and then makes the `%` formatting raise `TypeError`. That breaks the never-raises contract, which the removed f-string kept.\n  - Callers pass constants today, so exposure is low.\n  - Minimal fix: `_breadcrumb(f\"emit_generic: unknown action {action!r}\")`.\n- **P2-4. The public `emit_generic` lost its docstring.**\n  - Where: `.claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:473`.\n  - Scenario: the removed docstring told callers that `emit_generic` never raises, applies no redaction, and that free-text fields must be redacted before the call. `help()` and IDE hovers now show nothing, so a new caller loses the instruction to pre-redact.\n  - Minimal fix: copy the original docstring onto the facade function."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":823,"cache_read_input_tokens":214834,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":823},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05d43db1-9d87-44b2-ba52-8d3e41e19567","uuid":"5e328360-9a2a-4d20-b818-679ed72c6d0d","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:59:51.178Z","request_id":"req_011Ch77yJkhF1xXjfnoPHmZE"}
