only in annotations, which are not evaluated under `from __future__ import annotations` or as local-variable annotations.\n   - The spool-writer forensic emitter and the exit-handler hookup at import are kept (audit_emit.py:486-496).\n5. Python 3.9 and standard library: no 3.10+ syntax and no third-party imports in the destination code. FunctionType(code, globals, name, defaults, closure) works on 3.9.\n6. Condition 5: check_arbitration_kernel.py:312 lists `.claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/*`, and the facade itself is at :105.\n7. Condition 7 holds for audit_emit: the entry-point path is unchanged and the logic lives in _lib/_audit_emit_parts/.\n8. Fail direction (item 2): unchanged. The audit emit path fails open, and default-deny drops caller fields instead of writing them. Adopter blast radius (item 1): no hook is disabled, and no model or effort changes in this payload.\n\nNo declared condition is false against this payload, and I found no P0.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\nNone at P1.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\nP2-1 to P2-3 were already recorded at P2 in the signed rc.1 verdict claude-rc1-15; they are still present in this tree, unchanged. P2-4 is new.\n\nP2-1 (carried): decoy branches make two structure tests pass vacuously.\n- Where: .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:473-480.\n- Scenario: the facade's emit_generic has `if action == \"tool_call_lifecycle_recorded\"` and `if action == \"settings_tamper_detected\"`. Both do exactly what the fall-through line does. They exist only so that inspect.getsource(audit_emit.emit_generic) contains those comparisons, which .claude/hooks/tests/test_tool_lifecycle.py:541-563 and .claude/scripts/tests/test_ceo_boot_tamper_tripwires.py:521-525 require. The real scrub branches are generic_dispatch_04.py:62 and :159. If they are deleted, both tests stay green; the event would fall to default-deny, so fields would be lost, not leaked. The ghost-action guard test was updated correctly to walk _GENERIC_DISPATCH_HANDLERS.\n- Minimal fix: remove the decoys and make the two tests call emit_generic with a forbidden field, then assert the field is dropped and the enum values are coerced.\n\nP2-2 (carried): dead duplicate action registry.\n- Where: .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/actions.py:7-16, with actions_core.py and actions_extended.py (331 names).\n- Scenario: the install() roster does not include these files (audit_emit.py:415-452); the runtime registry is the literal at audit_emit.py:45-377. A maintainer who registers a new action in actions_core.py, which .claude/scripts/env-inventory.json points at, gets no runtime effect, and the action is silently dropped as unknown.\n- Minimal fix: delete actions*.py, or add a parity test pinning them equal to the facade literal.\n\nP2-3 (carried, extended): the unknown-action breadcrumb lost repr escaping and can now raise.\n- Where: .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/generic_dispatch_05.py:363.\n- Scenario: the removed code logged f\"emit_generic: unknown action {action!r}\"; the new code logs \"unknown audit action dropped: %s\" % action.\n  - An action string with a newline is written raw into the audit-log.errors sidecar, which is not HMAC-chained, so lines there can be forged.\n  - A tuple action is hashable, fails the membership test, and then makes the %-format raise TypeError. That breaks the never-raises contract, which the removed f-string kept.\n  - Callers pass constants today, so exposure is low.\n- Minimal fix: _breadcrumb(f\"emit_generic: unknown action {action!r}\").\n\nP2-4 (new): the public emit_generic lost its docstring.\n- Where: .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:473.\n- Scenario: the removed docstring documented the contract callers rely on: it never raises, it applies no redaction, and callers must redact free-text fields before the call. help() and IDE hovers now show nothing, so a new caller loses the instruction to pre-redact.\n- Minimal fix: copy the original docstring onto the facade function.","decision":"GO","sentence":"Every branch, enum, constant, helper and emitter this payload removes from audit_emit.py reappears unchanged and in the same order in _lib/_audit_emit_parts/, published through __all__ and bound to the facade's globals so names resolve and patch points still work; drop and default-deny behaviour is the same, the code is standard-library only and Python 3.9 compatible, condition 5's kernel row is present, and the only findings are P2 follow-ups, so there is no P0 and no false declared condition."}}}
